    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62904" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λήμ-η</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a humour that gathers in the
				corner of the eye, rheum</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>VM</u>
				19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Prog.</u>
				2
			</span></i>: in pl., <i>sore eyes</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				301
			</span></i> (v. Sch.): metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ τοῦ
				Πειραιέως λ.</span> the <i>eye-sore</i> of Piraeus, of
			Aegina, Pericles ap.<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1411a15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Per.</u>
				8
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρονικαὶ λῆμαι</span> old
			prejudices <i>that dim the mind's eye</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				581
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄψεως λ. ἡ δεισιδαιμονία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.1101c
				</span></i>
			. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάμας</span>.)</div>
